From f17e85e0083927b7d9cee516728c40cb66bbf62f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanyog Kale <skale@habana.ai>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2020 23:40:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SW-17444] preboot: goya2_arc: validate public key hash

This patch adds support to verify hash of public key received as
part of fit image against stored hash of public key.

In ARC based goya2 boot flow, arcboot performs hash validation for key
size of 392 bytes which includes modulus of 384 bytes and montgomery
information of 8 bytes.

Currently, preboot performs hash computation on complete public key
received as part of fit image and compare it against stored hash.
However, for goya2 ARC based flow, the hash needs to be computed with
modulus information of 384 bytes and montgomery information of 8 bytes.

Above mentioned hash computation support is added for goya2 ARC based
flow along with hash validation against stored hash.

Change-Id: I93a6f3178ed0213649c990aa0d8df7c975c9fbed
